Q: Confused over event coordinates reported and calculated from JScrollPane A: <p>To obtain the expected result, simply add the bar displacements to the coordinates of the detected point using the method <strong>scrollPane.get---ScrollBar().getValue();</strong> (replace <strong>---</strong> with <em>Vertical</em> or <em>Horizontal</em> as appropriate). Let's see how to apply this to your code:</p>
<pre><code>jScrollPane.addMouseListener( new MouseAdapter() {
   @Override
   public void mousePressed( MouseEvent mouseWheelEvent ) {
      Point eventPoint = mouseWheelEvent.getPoint();
      Point displacement = new Point( jScrollPane.getHorizontalScrollBar().getValue(),
                                      jScrollPane.getVerticalScrollBar().getValue() );
      System.out.println( &quot; eapp -&gt; &quot; + (eventPoint.x + displacement.x ) + 
                          &quot; &quot; + (eventPoint.y + displacement.y ) );            
   }
});
</code></pre>
